Producer:

Adds Data

Consumer:

Removes Data

Need synchronization.

Another Problem: Race Condition

Suppose:

Buffer contains:

[A B C]

Producer:

Insert D

Consumer:

Remove A

Both access buffer simultaneously.

Data may become corrupted.

Need:

Mutual Exclusion
Requirements

Producer–Consumer requires:

Mutual Exclusion

Only one thread accesses buffer at a time.

Synchronization

Producer waits if full.

Consumer waits if empty.

Semaphore Solution

Classic interview solution.

We use:

Mutex

Protects buffer.

Empty Semaphore

Counts empty slots.

Full Semaphore

Counts filled slots.

Example

Buffer size:

5

Initially:

empty = 5
full = 0
mutex = 1

Meaning:

5 Empty Slots
0 Filled Slots
Buffer Unlocked
Producer Flow

Before inserting:

wait(empty)

Check for free space.

Then:

wait(mutex)

Lock buffer.

Insert item.

Then:

signal(mutex)

Unlock buffer.

Then:

signal(full)

One more item available.

Visualization:

wait(empty)
wait(mutex)

Insert Item

signal(mutex)
signal(full)
Consumer Flow

Before removing:

wait(full)

Need data available.

Then:

wait(mutex)

Lock buffer.

Remove item.

Then:

signal(mutex)

Unlock.

Then:

signal(empty)

Free one slot.

Visualization:

wait(full)
wait(mutex)

Remove Item

signal(mutex)
signal(empty)
Example Walkthrough

Buffer Size:

5

Initial:

empty = 5
full = 0

Producer adds item.

Result:

empty = 4
full = 1

Producer adds second item.

empty = 3
full = 2

Eventually:

empty = 0
full = 5

Buffer Full.

Next producer:

wait(empty)

Blocked.

Consumer removes one item.

Now:

empty = 1
full = 4

Producer wakes.

System works correctly.

